mber of columns N.\n3. Compute document frequency for each column: count rows where matrix[i][j] != 0.\n4. Compute idf: for each j, if df[j]==0: idf_j = 0.0 else: idf_j = math.log(M / df[j]).\n5. Compute row_degree: sum of each row in original matrix.\n6. Compute weighted_matrix: for each i, row = [matrix[i][j] * idf[j] for j in range(N)].\n7. Return dict with keys \"idf\", \"row_degree\", \"weighted_matrix\".\n\nMake sure to convert to float where needed.\n\nReturn JSON-compatible: Python lists and floats.\n\nNow, write the Python code as a string for the implementation envelope.\n\nWe must not mutate case, so we can copy.\n\nWrite solve function.\n\nAlso note: The problem says \"may use only the Python standard library\". So math is fine.\n\nNow produce the JSON response with key \"implementation\" containing the source.\n\nWe need to escape the string properly.\n\nLet's write the code:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve(case):\n    matrix = case['matrix']\n    M = len(matrix)\n    N = len(matrix[0]) if M > 0 else 0\n    # compute document frequency\n    df = [0] * N\n    for row in matrix:\n        for j, val in enumerate(row):\n            if val != 0:\n                df[j] += 1\n    # idf\n    idf = []\n    for j in range(N):\n        if df[j] == 0:\n            idf.append(0.0)\n        else:\n            idf.append(math.log(M / df[j]))\n    # row_degree: sum of original row\n    row_degree = [sum(row) for row in matrix]\n    # weighted_matrix\n    weighted_matrix = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        wrow = [row[j] * idf[j] for j in range(N)]\n        weighted_matrix.append(wrow)\n    return {\n        \"idf\": idf,\n        \"row_degree\": row_degree,\n        \"weighted_matrix\": weighted_matrix\n    }\n```\n\nWe need to ensure that if matrix is empty? Not needed from fixtures.\n\nNow produce the JSON with implementation string. Use json.dumps to escape properly, but we must manually create the JSON object because we cannot use json module in the output